  "step_3": "The decision reason focuses on comparing the most favorable outcomes with the lowest probabilities and prefers the one with the higher payoff. The individual explicitly highlights the higher payoff of B (double the amount) as a key reason for preference, despite the lower probability, and justifies this by being willing to 'bet on luck' when both outcomes are desirable and financial need is low. This aligns with focusing on the most favorable, least probable outcome and preferring the one with the higher value. While the individual does not explicitly frame their reasoning in terms of 'least probable outcomes,' their attention to the rare, high-value outcome and preference for it matches the core logic of the decision reason. The justification is consistent with the rule of the reason, even if not articulated in technical terms.",
